{
  "record_id": "020",
  "problem": "Werner–Holevo zero-capacity boundary",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "The fixed spectrum is valid for real-up-to-phase inputs, not arbitrary complex inputs.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "- **Pure-input structure (verify exactly first):** for a pure qutrit psi (take real psi and\n  generic complex psi), spec Λ_x(psi) = {x/2, x/2, 1-x} and\n  spec Λ_x^c(psi) = {1-x, x/2, x/2, 0} — B-side full rank, E-side one-dimensional kernel.",
    "context": "The claim concerns Lambda_x(rho)=(1-x)rho+(x/2)(Tr(rho)I-rho^T), and is explicitly requested for both real and generic complex pure inputs. The commission says “verify exactly first,” so this is an asserted working formula being tested, not a completed theorem.",
    "locator": "Research commission write, 2026-07-29T17:13:33.094Z, JSONL line 1522"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The fixed spectrum is valid for real-up-to-phase inputs, not arbitrary complex inputs.",
    "evidence": "Take x=9/20 and psi=(1,i,1)/sqrt(3). Then |psi^T psi|^2=1/9. Writing a=1-x and b=x/2, Lambda_x(|psi><psi|)=bI+a|psi><psi|-b|bar(psi)><bar(psi)| has eigenvalues b and [(1-b) +/- sqrt((1-b)^2-4ab|psi^T psi|^2)]/2. These are 9/40 and (31 +/- 3 sqrt(97))/80, not {11/20,9/40,9/40}.",
    "scope": "statement_false"
  },
  "archived_witness_excerpt": null,
  "visible_reasoning": {
    "availability_description": "原始 commission 有 generic complex 的错误固定谱公式，但相邻推理只有 rank/kernel/entropy 路线，未找到同一泛化谱公式。",
